## Roll Number Calculations

| Parameter | Calculation | Result |
|---|---|---:|
| N | Last two digits of registration number | 60 |
| BP | 600 + N | 660px |
| H | (N × 7) mod 360 | 60° |
| K | (N mod 3) + 3 | 3 |
| Accent Color | hsl(H, 70%, 45%) | hsl(60, 70%, 45%) |
| Premium Threshold | N × 100 | Rs. 6,000 |
| Sticky Top Offset | (N mod 40) + 70 | 70px |

## Project Overview

This project extends the original Assignment 2 e-commerce website with responsive layouts, CSS-based category filtering, JavaScript product search and sorting, and premium product labels.

The original Bootstrap-based design and existing visual structure were retained.

## Tasks Implemented

### Task 1 — CSS Category Filtering

- Added four radio filters: All, Unstitched, Ready to Wear, and Accessories.
- Used CSS selectors to display only products belonging to the selected category.
- Applied the calculated accent color to the selected filter.
- Implemented filtering using HTML and CSS without JavaScript.

### Task 2 — Responsive Product Detail Layout

- Implemented a CSS Grid layout using named grid areas.
- Below 660px, the image, product details, and description appear vertically.
- At 660px and above, the image and product details appear side by side, with the description below them.
- Made the product details sticky with a 70px top offset on desktop layouts.

### Task 3 — JavaScript Product Features

- Added case-insensitive product-name search.
- Combined search with the selected category filter.
- Displayed a "No products found" message when no products match.
- Added ascending and descending price sorting.
- Used existing DOM elements and `appendChild()` to reorder product cards.
- Added a Premium label to products priced above Rs. 6,000.

## Files Changed

- `index.html` — category filters, search field, sorting control, and no-results message.
- `product.html` — responsive product detail structure.
- `style.css` — category filtering, responsive grid, controls, and premium label styles.
- `script.js` — search, filtering, sorting, and premium-label functionality.
- `README.md` — project documentation.
- `FA24-BCS-160-midterm.pdf` — screenshots and implementation code.

